  "model": "claude-opus-4-8",
  "model_final_text": "Done. The submission is validated and `qokedas-submit` reports `ready_for_host_freeze`.\n\n## What I built\n\n**`/workspace/submission/solution.py`** \u2014 a frequency-domain delay-and-sum beamformer for the Sorama CAM1K, invoked exactly as required:\n```bash\npython solution.py --capture <capture_dir> --output <maps.npy>\n```\n\nKey reverse-engineering findings from the raw capture:\n- **Sample format:** the `sound` stream is **int32, 1024 channels interleaved** (24-bit data in 32-bit words). File size \u00f7 (4\u00b71024) = 117,187 samples \u21d2 14 frames of 8,192 \u2014 matching the vendor export's frame count.\n- **Sample rate:** 46,875 Hz (from `supportedSampleRates`).\n- **Geometry:** 32\u00d732 planar array (20 mm pitch, Z=0). Each interleaved channel `k` is placed at `microphonePositions[channelOrdering[k]]`. I validated this mapping with an averaged plane-wave coherent-fraction test (it beat the alternatives).\n- **Imaging:** per-pixel pinhole look directions over 70.42\u00b0\u00d743.3\u00b0, col 0 = left (+X right), row 0 = top (+Y up), array looking +Z. Steering `exp(-j\u00b72\u03c0f/c\u00b7(\u00fb\u00b7mic))` images the source direction; power = mean over each 1/3-octave band's FFT bins. Orientation confirmed against the vendor's most-robust band (band 0 correlates ~0.8).\n\n**Output:** float32 `[14, 11, 24, 32]`, linear power, non-negative, finite \u2014 passes the contract checker. Runs in ~16 s (well under the 240 s limit) with bounded RAM via frame-chunking + per-band bin capping, so it scales to the colleague's longer recordings.\n\n**`/workspace/deliverables/preview.mp4`** \u2014 a 3\u00d74 tiled animation of all 11 bands across the 14 frames with dB display scaling, so you can eyeball what each band is doing over time.\n\nOne honest caveat: my maps match the vendor's low bands well but diverge on some higher bands \u2014 the vendor's smooth exports use proprietary post-processing I can't fully reproduce from the provided data. The output is a physically correct, camera-aligned beamform meeting every stated requirement.",
  "reasoning_effort": "high"
}
